    "fixture": true,
    "type": "answer_completed",
    "answer": "PEP 386 was superseded by PEP 440. PEP 440 says it addresses several limitations of the earlier versioning approach in PEP 345 and PEP 386, and that it supersedes PEP 386 even for metadata v1.2. One stated reason: it sorts top-level .devN releases ahead of alpha releases, because projects do not want developmental releases sorted between their release candidates and final releases. As of this corpus snapshot PEP 386 is Superseded and PEP 440 is Final.",
